      "index": "b17",
      "text": "Database sharding",
      "originalText": "Database sharding",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "autoResize": true,
      "baseline": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "YkaMvMI7xMEus80rnstc1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1531.9258930749274,
      "y": 2358.5445676583304,
      "width": 334,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1969795021,
      "version": 166,
      "versionNonce": 2125391628,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787144207106,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "b18",
      "text": "• Chat logs + order transaction records\n   split across DB instances by hash(user_id)\n• Ring + virtual nodes: adding capacity\n   moves ~1/N of the data, not all of it\n• Plain h(key) % N would remap nearly\n   every key whenever N changes\n• Same partitioning model as Cassandra\n   and DynamoDB",
      "originalText": "• Chat logs + order transaction records\n   split across DB instances by hash(user_id)\n• Ring + virtual nodes: adding capacity\n   moves ~1/N of the data, not all of it\n• Plain h(key) % N would remap nearly\n   every key whenever N changes\n• Same partitioning model as Cassandra\n   and DynamoDB",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "baseline": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "P0NuJ01qmEHpP8fW0s3cB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 635.9258930749274,
      "y": 2542.5445676583304,
      "width": 1214.0625,
      "height": 16.8,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#862e9c",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 631384711,
      "version": 168,
      "versionNonce": 141631224,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788373221462,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "b19",
      "text": "Ring + virtual nodes keep key movement bounded and load even on resize — the same mechanism behind Redis Cluster, Cassandra, DynamoDB and most CDNs.",
      "originalText": "Ring + virtual nodes keep key movement bounded and load even on resize — the same mechanism behind Redis Cluster, Cassandra, DynamoDB and most CDNs.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "autoResize": true,
      "baseline": 12
    },
